# ia-router · optional environment variables
#
# Copy this file as `.env` (cp .env.example .env) and fill in whatever you want to use.
# The real `.env` is in .gitignore: it is NEVER pushed to git. What is versioned is this example.
# A variable already defined in your environment (export ...) takes priority over `.env`.

# --- Artificial Analysis (opcional) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Adds SPEED (tokens per second) and PRICE for each model, and correct-answer benchmarks
# (coding and math indexes, GPQA, HLE…). Without this key the routing uses only Arena (accuracy) and the
# "speed" question is not offered.
#
# How to get it (free): create an account at https://artificialanalysis.ai/ and generate an API key
# (free plan: 1,000 requests per day). Paste it here, without quotes or spaces.
# It is used by `python3 cli.py metrics refresh` or when updating the metrics from the chat.
# It asks for attribution: the router already shows "Artificial Analysis (artificialanalysis.ai)" when it uses it.
ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY=

# --- Optional, for daily use -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder where your state is stored (downloaded metrics, priorities, history). Default: ~/.ia-router
# ROUTER_HOME=/path/to/another/folder

# Turns off colors and styles in the terminal.
# NO_COLOR=1
